WEBVTT

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.521
If intelligence grows stronger, why can we still move
toward a future we do not want?

00:00:03.541 --> 00:00:05.176
This short film introduces Meaning Intelligence.

00:00:05.196 --> 00:00:06.245
It does not replace capability.

00:00:06.265 --> 00:00:07.741
It asks where capability should lead.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.955
We are good at asking how.

00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:16.052
Meaning Intelligence asks why, for whom, and at what
scale.

00:00:16.072 --> 00:00:21.155
It studies directional judgment, not another ability
ranked alongside intelligence quotients.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:28.641
In the book's framework, meaning is a worthwhile relation
between action and a larger system.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.053
It is more than a feeling.

00:00:30.073 --> 00:00:34.510
A judgment names direction, value, and boundary, and
remains open to revision.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:41.875
Meaning potential describes the value distance between the
present state and an ideal direction.

00:00:41.895 --> 00:00:44.957
It is not a happiness score or a probability of success.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:47.655
It is dynamic, and still a construct to test.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:53.745
The book's mechanism has three modules: perception,
judgment, and action

00:00:53.765 --> 00:00:57.843
and four processes: identification, evaluation, decision,
and feedback.

00:00:57.863 --> 00:01:01.294
They are phases of one spiral cycle, not isolated boxes.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.885
A runnable agent puts the mechanism into context.

00:01:05.905 --> 00:01:11.459
It receives signals, interprets the situation, proposes a
direction, asks for human confirmation, and monitors
results.

00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:13.660
Critical choices remain traceable and vetoable.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.894
That is design, not proof of effectiveness.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:23.299
The six-layer stack moves from reducing load to
experiencing

00:01:23.319 --> 00:01:28.120
generating meaning, assessing value, choosing direction,
and recursive review.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:33.374
It is an E-zero engineering extension, not fixed canon,
and not independently tested.

00:01:33.394 --> 00:01:37.426
Its one-to-six labels are not the canon's one-to-three
labels.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:43.366
Meaning judgment spans five scales: individual,
organization, city, nation, and civilization.

00:01:43.386 --> 00:01:45.558
Their meaning logics cannot be reduced to one another.

00:01:45.578 --> 00:01:49.878
Coordination is not a weighted average; conflict calls for
recalibration from the meta-meaning level.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.774
A complete directional judgment names direction, value,
and boundary.

00:01:56.794 --> 00:01:58.989
Looking only at gains can hide relational costs.

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:01.250
Looking only at now can forget long-term effects.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.361
Boundaries make choices open to scrutiny.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:10.205
When a meaning structure fails, active zeroing is not
surrender.

00:02:10.225 --> 00:02:12.239
It deliberately resets key premises.

00:02:12.259 --> 00:02:14.611
Reflection rewrites the next cycle's input

00:02:14.631 --> 00:02:18.560
so the loop does not repeat unchanged; it continues with
revision.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.004
Begin with three questions: Is what I am doing worthwhile?

00:02:23.024 --> 00:02:23.754
For whom?

00:02:23.774 --> 00:02:24.628
Within what boundary?

00:02:24.648 --> 00:02:26.460
Write down the evidence and the uncertainty.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.927
Meaning Intelligence offers no single right answer, only a
clearer way to ask.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.414
May every convergence move toward what is worthwhile.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:38.167
Understanding Meaning Intelligence is not forcing the
world into one conclusion.

00:02:38.187 --> 00:02:39.991
It is keeping the courage to judge, revise, and stop.

00:02:40.011 --> 00:02:40.830
Thank you.
